{
  "dom_id": "step-e7654",
  "name": "Example: Solving an Inequality Involving a Cube Root",
  "problem": "Solve the inequality $\\sqrt[3]{x+3} + 1 \\geq  0.$",
  "worked_solution": "Isolating the cubic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{x+3}+1 & \\ge 0 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{x+3} & \\ge -1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we cube both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\sqrt[3]{x+3})}^{3} & \\ge {(-1)}^{3} \\\\ x+3 & \\ge -1 \\\\ x & \\ge -4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
